Good — I'm in, and happy to take a share.

One suggestion on what the list should be, so it stays useful and short: **the decisions the professor actually has to make**, not a readiness audit of each of our sections. If we each post "here's where my part stands", it turns into seven status reports for a half-hour meeting and we spend it reading rather than deciding. What I'd propose we collect instead:

- items that genuinely need a call **before Monday's session** (by definition, the 24th is too late for these — so they're either decided in the thread or raised with the professor another way);
- items for the 24th itself, with a one-line question each so he can come prepared;
- anything cross-cutting (room, deadlines, who publishes what, when).

Sarah — if you're happy to keep it in one place, I'll draft the open questions from my side in that shape. John — take the lead on the list itself; I'll add mine and check nothing's missing. And Alvarez — noted, we won't copy you unless something changes the calendar.
